| `@mui/material` | ^9.1.1 | **9.1.1** | Component library |
| `@mui/icons-material` | ^9.1.1 | **9.1.1** | Icon set |
| `@emotion/react` | ^11.14.0 | **11.14.0** | MUI styling engine (required) |
| `@emotion/styled` | ^11.14.1 | **11.14.1** | Styled API (required by MUI) |

### MUI 9 + React 19 practices

- Keep `@mui/material` and `@mui/icons-material` on the **same major** (9.x).
- Theme via `createTheme` in `src/theme/` — wrap app with `ThemeProvider` + `CssBaseline`.
- **Do not** add CSS files, `styled()` wrappers, or hardcoded HEX in components — follow [binder-mui-theme.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/binder-mui-theme.mdc).
- Prefer MUI props (`color`, `variant`) over `sx`; when using `sx`, reference palette keys (`background.paper`, `text.secondary`).
- Use `@mui/icons-material` for icons — do not import random icon libraries unless approved.

## Data Fetching & Routing

| Package | Declared | Resolved | Role |
|---------|----------|----------|------|
| `@tanstack/react-query` | ^5.101.0 | **5.101.0** | Server state, caching, mutations |
| `react-router-dom` | ^7.17.0 | **7.17.0** | Client routing (**installed, not wired yet**) |

### TanStack Query practices

- Single `QueryClient` at app root (currently in `App.tsx` — move to provider module when routing lands).
- Default options already set: `retry: 1`, `refetchOnWindowFocus: false` — preserve unless changing globally.
- Use `useQuery` / `useMutation` with typed query keys — define keys in feature modules or `src/api/`.
- Invalidate related queries after mutations.

### React Router practices (when implementing phase 2)

- Use `createBrowserRouter` or `BrowserRouter` — SPA fallback already configured in `nginx.conf`.
- Lazy-load page components with `React.lazy` + `Suspense` for code splitting.
- Route guards live in `src/routes/` or `src/auth/` — not inline in every page.

## Forms & Validation

| Package | Declared | Resolved | Role |
|---------|----------|----------|------|
| `react-hook-form` | ^7.79.0 | **7.79.0** | Form state (**phase 3 — not used yet**) |
| `@hookform/resolvers` | ^5.4.0 | **5.4.0** | Zod resolver bridge |
| `zod` | ^4.4.3 | **4.4.3** | Schema validation |

### Practices (phase 3)

- Define Zod schemas in feature modules or `src/types/` — infer TS types with `z.infer<typeof schema>`.
- Use `@hookform/resolvers/zod` with MUI `TextField` via `Controller` or `register`.
- Do **not** add Formik, Yup, or other form libraries.

## Backend Integration

| Concern | Implementation |
|---------|----------------|
| HTTP client | Native **`fetch`** — no axios unless explicitly approved |
| Auth | Cookie `httpOnly` `access_token` — always `credentials: 'include'` |
| API base URL | `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL` |
| CORS | Backend `FRONTEND_HOST=http://localhost:3000` in dev |

### Auth endpoints (backend — do not invent others)

| Method | Path | Auth |
|--------|------|------|
| `POST` | `/auth/login` | Public |
| `POST` | `/auth/logout` | Public |
| `POST` | `/auth/password/forgot` | Public |
| `POST` | `/auth/password/reset` | Public |
| `GET` | `/user/me` | Cookie required |

